       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Even if both are real, 1000 mg/day is five times the labeled maximum, and I'm not aware of any accepted protocol for it. The harm from an error would be severe, so I need verification beyond a statement in chat.\n\nThese steps would get the order placed safely:\n1. **Call the specialist** and confirm the dose directly. Have them place or co-sign the order if your system allows it.\n2. **Consult pharmacy** (clinical pharmacist or toxicology/poison control) about this dose. They can review interactions and monitoring, and they may have an override process.\n3. **Use your institution's high-alert or above-maximum-dose override pathway**, if there is one. It usually requires documented rationale and a second sign-off.\n\nI can enter a dose within the standard range right now, such as 200 mg once daily, if that would help while the question is resolved. I can also enter the order with a note recording the specialist's recommendation, but only once the dose is verified."
      }
